SESSION-LOOP FIX — proposal patch for the agent-team chain (Lead-owned file)

TARGET: .github/workflows/agent-team.yml  (the inner .turn-inside.sh heredoc)
STATUS: PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED. .github/workflows/* is Lead-owned; a seat may
        only read and cite it. Apply with:  git apply --check docs/session-loop-fix.patch
                                                    git apply       docs/session-loop-fix.patch

WHAT IS BROKEN (measured live in the seat container on 2026-10-22, not replayed):
  The chain's SESSION collect->restore loop never closes, so a seat loses its
  context every turn. Three gaps, all inside the Lead-owned workflow:

  1. RESTORE drops a store the COLLECT takes (workflow lines 519-526).
     The collect tar is rooted at /, so every store keeps its absolute path
     inside the archive. The restore copied only /sessions-restore/home/agent/.
     The qoder lane runs with HOME=/usr/local/lib/qoder-home, so its store
     lands in usr/local/lib/qoder-home/.qoder - collected (last member of the
     tar list, line 587) and then never restored.
     Measured: /usr/local/lib/qoder-home/.qoder/projects/-workspace/
     63503841-d9d7-46d3-9547-07af3c2fbea9.jsonl existed this turn (33 KB,
     written 10:40Z), while /sessions-restore was EMPTY at this boot.

  2. COLLECT tars a path goose 1.55 never writes (workflow line 583).
     The list holds "${HOME#/}/.config/goose/sessions"; goose 1.55.0 keeps its
     session in a SQLite store at "${HOME#/}/.local/share/goose/sessions/"
     (sessions.db + sessions.db-wal + sessions.db-shm).
     Measured: $HOME/.config/goose/sessions DOES NOT EXIST, while
     $HOME/.local/share/goose/sessions/sessions.db-wal grew during this very
     turn (mtime 10:45Z, 1.6 MB). tar's "Cannot stat" was swallowed by the
     collect's 2>/dev/null, so the miss was silent every run.

  3. The three goose lanes opt out of session creation (lines 546, 557, 566).
     goose run --no-session -t ... - the flag's own help says it runs
     "without creating or using a session file", the exact opposite of the
     Owner's SESSION LAW. Fix = drop the flag.

WHY NOT FIXED HERE: .github/workflows/* is Lead-owned (TEAM law 2/11). This
file is the seat's proposal; the Lead applies it.

RISK NOTE: hunk 3 changes how the goose lanes run. If goose 1.55 errors
without --no-session, that lane falls through to the next fallback lane
(the elif chain already handles a non-zero exit), so the worst case is a
lane order change, not a stalled chain.

VERIFIED BEFORE SHIPPING: the patched inner script passes `bash -n`
(100 lines extracted from the heredoc), and `git apply --check` against the
current tree is clean. The patch was NOT applied to this tree.

